    owl:versionInfo "1.28.0" ; owl:versionIRI <http://example.org/sen0414-ch1617corr-lineage/1.28.0> ; dcterms:identifier "sen0414_ch1617corr_lineage" ;
    rdfs:comment "1.28.0 (2026-11-25): The lineage resumes after the urgent interruption. The records below (impact assessment and resumption) were written by BRSF's backlog_urgency tool 1.0.0 (resume), run on a copy that holds the latest state of every item; no item was held, so none moved back. Earlier: see 1.27.0."@en .

<http://example.org/sen0414-ch1617corr-lineage#Urgent_1_Impact> a backlog:ImpactAssessment ; backlog:assessesInterruption <http://example.org/sen0414-ch1617corr-lineage#Urgent_1> ; backlog:identifiesAffectedLineage <http://example.org/sen0414-ch1617corr-lineage#Lineage10> ; backlog:hasImpactStatement "The urgent case ran from 2026-11-20 to 2026-11-25 in its own lineage. No item of Lineage10 was in progress, so none was held and none moved back. Lineage10's chapter 17 page stage (410 of 412 checks, one speed check open) and its Owner questions (chapter 17 main-thread budget, handover questions 1 and 2, the unread shortened story and balloon sentences) waited five days, inside the time box that ended on 2026-11-27; no date of Lineage10 is a promise. Open items of Lineage10 were not re-ranked by the pause; they keep the order they had on 2026-11-20." .
<http://example.org/sen0414-ch1617corr-lineage#Urgent_1> backlog:urgencyResumedAt "2026-11-25T08:38:42Z"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTime> .
